WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:16.392
Dr. Dolittle and Polynesia arrived on the beach.

2
00:00:17.213 --> 00:00:20.776
Tommy was so happy to see the doctor that he began to cry.

3
00:00:20.796 --> 00:00:24.299
"Hush, now," the doctor said, comforting him.

4
00:00:24.319 --> 00:00:26.581
"It's good to have you back, Dr.

5
00:00:26.621 --> 00:00:29.664
Dolittle," Charles said as he brushed away a tear.

6
00:00:31.424 --> 00:00:35.625
"We must get going before the natives find you are missing," said Polynesia.

7
00:00:35.645 --> 00:00:37.946
"Will the people be all right?"

8
00:00:38.326 --> 00:00:40.807
the doctor asked, looking back toward the huts.

9
00:00:40.827 --> 00:00:43.507
"Of course," answered Long Arrow.

10
00:00:43.527 --> 00:00:45.528
"They already have a chief.

11
00:00:46.208 --> 00:00:48.369
Do not worry, I will explain to them."

12
00:00:49.529 --> 00:00:50.809
"You're not coming with us?"

13
00:00:51.089 --> 00:00:52.670
the doctor said in surprise.

14
00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.931
"I'm afraid not, my friend," the Indian said sadly.

15
00:00:56.951 --> 00:00:59.352
"My journey is different from yours.

16
00:00:59.812 --> 00:01:02.393
You must go your way, and I must go mine."

17
00:01:03.073 --> 00:01:05.135
The two men did not speak for a minute.

18
00:01:05.155 --> 00:01:07.576
"Will we ever meet again?"

19
00:01:07.836 --> 00:01:08.457
asked Dr.

20
00:01:08.497 --> 00:01:14.581
Dolittle. "As long as the eagles soar, our paths shall cross," replied Long Arrow.

21
00:01:15.762 --> 00:01:17.743
A loud splash came from the waters.

22
00:01:17.763 --> 00:01:20.545
"He is here," Polynesia said.

23
00:01:20.565 --> 00:01:21.706
"Who is?"

24
00:01:22.026 --> 00:01:22.767
asked the doctor.

25
00:01:22.787 --> 00:01:25.028
"Remember what the fidgit said?"

26
00:01:25.508 --> 00:01:27.730
Tommy grabbed the doctor's hand excitedly.

27
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.692
"He spoke about the great glass sea snail?"

28
00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.953
Tommy led the doctor toward the edge of the water.

29
00:01:35.653 --> 00:01:40.015
Dr. Dolittle stopped in his tracks and gasped at the creature before him.

30
00:01:40.776 --> 00:01:44.457
It was an enormous snail, the size of two large houses.

31
00:01:45.217 --> 00:01:49.019
Its shell was transparent and shone like a million diamonds.

32
00:01:49.039 --> 00:01:51.060
"It's beautiful!"

33
00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:52.340
sighed the doctor.

34
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.701
"How did you find it?"

35
00:01:54.721 --> 00:02:02.541
"When we told Long Arrow you wanted to learn shellfish language," explained Tommy, "Long Arrow went in search

36
00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:03.241
of the snail."

37
00:02:03.861 --> 00:02:06.042
Dr. Dolittle smiled at Long Arrow.

38
00:02:06.062 --> 00:02:10.164
"Now you can learn the language on your way back home," said Tommy.

39
00:02:10.184 --> 00:02:14.366
"What? Will the snail come with us?"

40
00:02:14.846 --> 00:02:16.407
the doctor said, confused.

41
00:02:17.147 --> 00:02:20.489
The snail let out a loud groan and shook its huge body.

42
00:02:21.189 --> 00:02:23.830
The bottom of its shell came away from its body.

43
00:02:24.531 --> 00:02:27.272
Dr. Dolittle's eyes grew big with excitement.

44
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.442
"You and your friends can ride inside the shell," Long Arrow explained.

45
00:02:33.223 --> 00:02:35.944
"The snail will take you on an underwater journey."

46
00:02:37.225 --> 00:02:39.646
Dr. Dolittle wiped a tear from his eye.

47
00:02:39.666 --> 00:02:42.008
"How can I ever thank you?"

48
00:02:42.308 --> 00:02:43.448
he said with emotion.

49
00:02:44.309 --> 00:02:46.010
"You are my dearest friend."

50
00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:48.892
Dr. Dolittle blew his nose.

51
00:02:48.912 --> 00:02:52.974
"You have made all my dreams come true."

52
00:02:54.935 --> 00:02:56.616
Tommy felt a lump in his throat.

53
00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.480
He looked around the island.

54
00:02:59.041 --> 00:03:00.641
The sun was starting to come up.

55
00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:05.923
He realized that he had learned much more on this voyage than he had ever expected.

56
00:03:06.543 --> 00:03:10.484
But he also realized how much he missed his parents and Puddleby.

57
00:03:11.184 --> 00:03:12.564
He was ready to go home.

58
00:03:15.025 --> 00:03:17.726
It was very sad to say good-bye to Long Arrow.

59
00:03:18.386 --> 00:03:20.687
He had a gift for each of his new friends.

60
00:03:21.427 --> 00:03:25.288
To Charles he gave a beautiful stone with a red dot in the middle.

61
00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.542
To Tommy he gave a large eagle's feather.

62
00:03:29.302 --> 00:03:32.084
Tommy wore it in his hair, just like Long Arrow.

63
00:03:33.144 --> 00:03:36.946
For Polynesia, Long Arrow had a tiny necklace made of flowers.

64
00:03:37.727 --> 00:03:39.668
She wore it proudly around her neck.

65
00:03:40.809 --> 00:03:42.490
And finally, to Dr.

66
00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.631
Dolittle Long Arrow gave his pouch.

67
00:03:45.371 --> 00:03:49.554
"I can't accept this," the doctor said, his voice choking.

68
00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:56.445
"It is my most treasured item," said the Indian, "and I want my most treasured friend to have

69
00:03:56.485 --> 00:04:00.287
it." The two friends cried as they finally said good-bye.

70
00:04:02.528 --> 00:04:06.009
Dr. Dolittle and his friends climbed into the sea snail's shell.

71
00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:09.231
Inside the shell, it was comfortably warm.

72
00:04:10.011 --> 00:04:14.613
There were no chairs, but Tommy found that the snail's back was soft to sit on.

73
00:04:15.294 --> 00:04:16.394
He looked outside.

74
00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:20.236
It felt strange to view the world from inside a shell.

75
00:04:22.616 --> 00:04:26.118
After everyone was settled in, the snail groaned once again.

76
00:04:26.918 --> 00:04:30.861
Its shell locked in place and slowly it moved into the water.

77
00:04:31.661 --> 00:04:36.964
Dr. Dolittle and his friends waved to Long Arrow as they disappeared below the waves.

78
00:04:36.984 --> 00:04:39.765
"Now the real voyage begins!"

79
00:04:40.286 --> 00:04:41.546
Charles shouted joyfully.

80
00:04:42.227 --> 00:04:45.628
Yes, returning home was yet another adventure.

81
00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.852
After returning to Puddleby, Tommy's life changed quite a bit.

82
00:04:52.616 --> 00:04:54.997
He could now speak more animal languages.

83
00:04:55.737 --> 00:04:58.678
He was no longer afraid of any kind of animal.

84
00:04:59.418 --> 00:05:03.139
And he was certain that he wanted to be an animal doctor when he grew up.

85
00:05:03.999 --> 00:05:05.860
But some things would never change.

86
00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.681
"Tommy! Come listen to this!"

87
00:05:10.181 --> 00:05:14.963
the doctor would shout excitedly, pulling his head out of the shellfish tank.

88
00:05:15.883 --> 00:05:17.003
"I think I've got it!"

89
00:05:17.743 --> 00:05:20.212
Whenever Charles came to visit, Dr.

90
00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:22.673
Dolittle and his friends would talk about their trip.

91
00:05:23.053 --> 00:05:26.814
The other pets never got tired of hearing all the exciting stories.

92
00:05:27.354 --> 00:05:29.735
But Tommy was ready for a new voyage.

93
00:05:31.236 --> 00:05:33.636
During one of Charles' visits, Dr.

94
00:05:33.676 --> 00:05:35.557
Dolittle looked at Tommy and winked.

95
00:05:36.237 --> 00:05:37.477
It seemed as if Dr.

96
00:05:37.517 --> 00:05:38.898
Dolittle were ready too.

97
00:05:40.738 --> 00:05:42.879
Tommy thought of places they could travel.

98
00:05:43.599 --> 00:05:45.260
It didn't matter where they went.

99
00:05:46.021 --> 00:05:47.925
As long as Tommy was with Dr.

100
00:05:47.965 --> 00:05:51.011
Dolittle, every voyage would be an adventure.
